---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Vitor Sacramento — Data engineering and geospatial intelligence" description="Portfolio of Vitor Sacramento: data engineering, geospatial AI, environmental intelligence and software systems.">
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Data engineering · Geospatial AI · Climate tech</p>
        <h1>Building intelligent systems from complex data.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Vitor Sacramento works at the intersection of data platforms, artificial intelligence, geospatial analysis and environmental intelligence.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/projects/">Explore projects</a><a class="button secondary" href="/about/">Professional profile</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="signal" role="img" aria-label="Abstract contour lines representing data and terrain"></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Core practice</p><h2>From raw signals to dependable systems.</h2></div><p class="lead">A portfolio organized around the work itself: data foundations, spatial context, applied intelligence and software delivery.</p></div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card"><span class="index">01 / DATA</span><h3>Data engineering & governance</h3><p>Data platforms, spatial databases, quality controls and reproducible processing.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><span class="index">02 / GEO</span><h3>Geospatial & environmental intelligence</h3><p>Geoprocessing, remote sensing, WebGIS and environmental data products.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><span class="index">03 / AI</span><h3>AI & machine learning</h3><p>Applied models, time series and computer vision grounded in observable evidence.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><span class="index">04 / SOFTWARE</span><h3>Software engineering & automation</h3><p>APIs, local-first tools, web applications and operational automation.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Publication standard</p><h2>Evidence before claims.</h2>
      <div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><strong>Audited</strong><span>Every published project traces back to code and tests.</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>Approved</strong><span>Private or corporate work is excluded without permission.</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>Reproducible</strong><span>Unverified instructions are labeled as such.</span></div></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
